Fresh portable validation passed in run 1795618492489171106-3014915.
An initial native smoke exposed a one-tick error in its synthetic
release timing; the corrected smoke rejects the primary edge at the
actual aerial landing while retaining the 84-pixel displacement.
The optimized 3,224,784-byte build passed adaptive touch smoke with
the verified 88-pose catalogue. All 600 movement and 60 combat
submissions met the 16.667 ms host-work budget; mean submission work
was 108.848 and 85.168 microseconds, respectively. Lifetime peak
RSS was 88,268,800 bytes. This remains offscreen evidence only.

One-tick directional pulses in all four isolated ground attacks
confirmed the distinction between the displayed pose and movement
recovery. Up at offset 19 matched all 101 control frames; at 20
it diverged. Left at offset 18 changed the actor trace without
flipping its facing; at 19 it matched every control frame. Marge's
held-left and held-right comparisons from offsets 1 and 17
showed downward rounding of the observed quarter-pixel drift.
The preview retains that fractional remainder during the attack
and through offset 18, then blocks displacement and turning
