button actions. Held directions resume on the next admitted
walking tick. Inline tests cover four-station ground drift, retained
facing, both turn-only landings, and the forward aerial direction
lock. Moving and interrupted original recovery are not fully
established.

Fresh portable validation passed in run 1795618985483698513-3092891.
The 3,225,872-byte optimized preview passed adaptive offscreen
OpenGL ES touch smoke with the verified 88-pose catalogue. All
600 movement and 60 combat submissions met the 16.667 ms
host-work budget. Mean submission work was 110.313 and 85.773
microseconds, respectively; lifetime peak RSS was 88,780,800 bytes.
Physical presentation and full original gameplay remain unverified.

A further directional probe isolated aerial attack takeoff in all four
characters. A one-tick Left pulse on the attack edge changed the
original trajectory; the same pulse at offset one matched all 101
object-DMA frames of each control. Marge also rejected the pulses at
offsets two and ten. Leftward travel used the same four-pixel stride
until the observed boundary. Stationary special Left pulses at offset
ten changed all four characters' facing without changing their
